-- title:
--   Good off-branch point reading a non-node place, q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 3$ and a nonzero level $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`). Write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   The data concerning level $M'$ in characteristic $q$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ is given (a place being a proper valuation subring containing the base field whose ring is a principal ideal ring), and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`: those $w$ which are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to$ `Place.ResidueField w` is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt` at the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in `ssJSet q κ`, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves have trivial $q$-torsion in the sense of `ssJSet`. The inclusion `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, where the latter is the geometric function field of level $q^2M'$ with subgroup `levelH q M'`. A `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is given: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, the condition that $a\in A$ is equivalent to the image of $a$ lying in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with compatibility of residues over $A$, the scaling axiom that every nonzero element can be rescaled by a constant into the integers with nonzero residue, and a place map preserving degrees and compatible with `Finsupp.mapDomain` on divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, viewed as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   The Igusa and supersingular charts. An element $\zeta$ of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is fixed, together with families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}} : \mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q) \to$ valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), and $O_{\mathrm{SS}} : W \to$ valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'`. The clauses on them are: `hIg_inf`, which identifies $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ (for `lineInfty q`) as the Gauss ring, namely $f$ lies in it precisely when $f\,y = x$ for Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero coefficientwise reduction; `hIg`, which states that every line $\ell$ is of the form `redQ q γ • lineInfty q` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which states that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. For the supersingular rings: `hSS_A` says that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over` says that if $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ is integral wherever the image of `jq` is (at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}\,f$) and if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation ring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr` provides, for each $s$, an element $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t - a$ a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   The Igusa prolongation. A `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2M') (levelH q M')` is given (a valuation subring with a surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue field, and satisfying the same rescaling axiom), subject to `hR`: $R.\mathrm{integers} = O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O`: an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   The arithmetic data. An element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q} \cap A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ is fixed. A subfield $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ are given such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` requires every $a \in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. An auxiliary prime $\ell \ne q$ with $\ell \ge 3$ and $\ell \nmid M'$ is fixed, together with $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (that is, $x \in A_1$ iff $x \in A$), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and quantifies over all intermediate fields $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the constants `adjoin k₀ (range (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M')))` is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the image of $K'$, the vanishing of $\sum_i c_i a_i$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and that $F_0$ contains every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series lies in the image of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, i.e. has rational coefficients.
--
--   Put $T_1 :=$ `adjoin k₀ (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M') '' K₁) ⊔ F₀`. The conclusion quantifies further over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is compatible with the inclusions $A_1 \subseteq K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, over an element $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the image under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`, with $j_1 \ne 0$, and over a finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2M') (levelH q M')` such that: every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ has its image in `fieldBar q M'` inside $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue equal to $j$ applied to its $R_0$-residue; and $Q \in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ holds precisely when there is $s \in W$ with $g \in s.\mathrm{toValuationSubring} \iff j(g) \in Q.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$ for all $g$.
--
--   On the scheme $\mathfrak X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $X_{\mathrm{Fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin A₁ T₁ j₁` and $X_{\infty} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf A₁ T₁ j₁` along the middle chart, the following predicates are introduced. For $x \in \mathfrak X$ and $f \in T_1$: `InStalk x f` holds when for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ mapping to $x$ under `ιFin` there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $fh = g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for $X_\infty$, `ιInf` and `chartAlgInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the extra requirement $g \in y$ in both charts. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ less than $1$ exactly when `InMax x f`; this predicate is introduced in the statement but does not occur in the asserted formula. Next, `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: the image of $x$ under `toBase` is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; every $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$; for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$, each $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a nonunit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in the prime $y$; the same for $X_\infty$ and `chartAlgInf`; and for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\,$`jChartFin`$\,) \notin$ `ssJSet q Ω`. Further, `Reads x Q` holds when every $f$ with `InStalk x f` has its image in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $R$-residue lying in the valuation subring of $Q$ and being a nonunit of that ring exactly when `InMax x f`. Finally, `OffBranch x` holds when for every line $\ell \ne$ `lineInfty q`, for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$ there is $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` with image a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and $b \notin y$, and likewise for every $y$ of $X_\infty$ with `chartAlgInf`.
--
--   The assertion is: for every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2M') (levelH q M')` with $Q \notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ there exists a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X$ such that `GoodPt x`, `OffBranch x` and `Reads x Q` all hold.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ instance of the existence half of the centring-and-reading step on the Igusa leg of the semistable covering: each place of the reduced Igusa function field that is not a node coming from a supersingular place of level $M'$ is read at a closed point of the two-chart integral model which lies on the special fibre, is not over a supersingular $j$-invariant, and meets no Igusa branch other than the one at infinity. It feeds the combined uniqueness-and-existence statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three), and through it the semistable covering of the modular curve at $q = 3$.
